  "reason": "The records repeatedly describe molecular-dynamics tensile deformation of the closely related FCC CoCrFeNiMn/Cantor-type alloy over a wide temperature range, including the same 10^8 s^-1 rate, and separately establish loading at rates up to 10^10 s^-1. They also connect yielding and plastic flow to partial-dislocation nucleation, stacking faults, local HCP-associated structures, stress drops, and thermally enhanced nucleation with reduced strength. Thus an expert could plausibly propose the later temperature-, rate-, and orientation-dependent tensile simulations and their partial-dislocation/stacking-fault mechanism. The exact quaternary FeNiCrMn bulk model, vacancy-cluster nucleation sites, orientation ranking, rate-insensitive yield strength, and absence of twinning or bulk FCC-HCP transformation are not directly anticipated, but they are refinements rather than a substantial new intervention concept."
